{
  "_comment": [
    "Third-party files the documentation serves from its own _static/vendor (no CDN, no Google Fonts:",
    " residual and 'Docs fonts'). Each package is an npm tarball pinned by",
    "version and by its registry integrity (sha512, verified before extraction by docs/site/vendor/fetch.py).",
    "Only the listed paths are copied. The fonts are the @fontsource versions of web/package-lock.json, so",
    "the site and the docs ship the same faces. To upgrade: change version, tarball and integrity together",
    "(https://registry.npmjs.org/<name>/<version> gives dist.tarball and dist.integrity).",
    "Every package names its licence (SPDX) and ships its licence text next to its files: 'LICENSE' in",
    "'copy', or, for a tarball without one, 'licence_from' (a vendored LICENSE of the same project, copied",
    "to <dest>/LICENSE). THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md lists them all (tests/infra/test_licences.py)."
  ],
  "packages": {
    "mathjax": {
      "version": "4.1.3",
      "licence": "Apache-2.0",
      "tarball": "https://registry.npmjs.org/mathjax/-/mathjax-4.1.3.tgz",
      "integrity": "sha512-BN/8Pkgn7G1pIDYJqd9md+JHsE/jydSYbyOZnSdSA0WziuVO8mRxdYiWFumkVVly/8U+hm9DpIIoWuvySverzw==",
      "dest": "mathjax",
      "copy": [
        "tex-chtml.js",
        "input",
        "output",
        "ui",
        "a11y",
        "adaptors",
        "sre",
        "LICENSE"
      ]
    },
    "@mathjax/mathjax-newcm-font": {
      "version": "4.1.3",
      "licence": "Apache-2.0",
      "tarball": "https://registry.npmjs.org/@mathjax/mathjax-newcm-font/-/mathjax-newcm-font-4.1.3.tgz",
      "integrity": "sha512-gzAB3dFHilHX1l5x2xUqRL+1jDQt3Fyza1DkEMVXWC4E8SvsGdlgEza47HYi2WhVcgfkvf4zgUGzuhbq3Pjlew==",
      "dest": "@mathjax/mathjax-newcm-font",
      "copy": [
        "chtml.js",
        "chtml",
        "package.json"
      ],
      "licence_from": "mathjax/LICENSE",
      "licence_note": "The 4.1.3 tarball has no LICENSE file; its package.json declares Apache-2.0, the licence of MathJax, whose text is copied from the mathjax package of the same release."
    },
